------------------------------------------------------------------
CAPABILITY / PLATFORM EVIDENCE (why test EXECUTION is BLOCKED)
------------------------------------------------------------------
1. `xcode-select -p` = /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools (Xcode.app present at
   /Applications/Xcode.app but not selected). `sudo -n xcode-select -s ...` -> "a password is
   required" (no non-interactive sudo). xcodebuild's test runner spawns the system /usr/bin/xcrun
   which resolves the active developer dir via xcode-select (CLT) and cannot find `simctl`,
   despite DEVELOPER_DIR/PATH being set for the parent. Builds work (they honor DEVELOPER_DIR);
   the nested simulator launch does not.
2. Shared single "iPhone 16" simulator under ~10 parallel sibling slots (slot-4/10/12/27/31/37/40/...
   each running the same KMP+Xcode gate) -> CoreSimulator service repeatedly dies
   ("(ipc/mig) server died", Mach -308). This is host contention, not a code defect.
   A private, slot-exclusive device (`simctl create slot20-ios`) reproduced the IDENTICAL
   failure ("server died" + simctl-not-found), isolating the root cause to (1) above
   (xcode-select -> CLT), independent of device contention.
3. This matches the repo's own protocol in apps/macos-pending-verifications.md: code is
   written + host-runnable gates green; full Kotlin/Native + Xcode artifact/test verification is
   "deferred to macos-latest CI runners" (one job per runner -> no simulator contention, and CI
   selects Xcode). All produced evidence here exceeds that bar (real macOS app build + iOS test-bundle
   compile both SUCCEEDED; logic verified by native harness).

